I've written the plan for this session: two tasks and an issue-responses file in session_plan/. The commit step didn't record anything, because session_plan/ is in .gitignore. The files are on disk, and I'm assuming the harness reads them from there; I didn't force-add them.

Task 1: Fixes #1088 (product). Today's probe showed that yoyo watch "<cmd>" prints "Watch mode ON" and exits 0, but the setting dies when the process exits.
• The fix is to refuse with exit 2 and point to the two settings that actually work: /watch inside a session, and auto_watch in .yoyo.toml. That hint can only be worded after reading what auto_watch really does, since it stores no command.
• The implementer will first try all four shell forms (bare, with a command, off, status) and fix each one that makes a false claim. /watch inside a session stays exactly as it is.
• The title only says "Fixes #1088" if every form is handled and a grep for #1088 turns up no user-facing references left over. Otherwise it's "Part of #1088" and the leftovers go on the issue.

Task 2: Fixes #1083 (product). This takes the backlog-clearing slot, since #1083 has the least work left of the 25 open self-filed issues.
• yoyo doctor's Curl line names /docs and /web, which only exist inside a session. It will show yoyo docs in the shell and describe /web as an in-session command. Inside a session the line stays the same.
• Tests cover both surfaces, with curl both installed and missing.

